{title: 511 - I Know Whom I Have Believed}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #511 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 511}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I know not why God’s [G]wondrous [D]grace
To me He [G]hath [D]made [A]known,
[A7]Nor [D]why, unworthy, [G]Christ in [D]love
Re[A]deemed me [A7]for His [D]own.
But “I [G]know whom I have be[D]lieved,
and am per[A]suaded that His is [D]able
To [G]keep that which I’ve com[D]mitted
Unto [A]Him a[A7]gainst that [D]day.”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]But "I know whom [G]I have believed, and am [D]persuaded that His is able
[G]To keep that [D]which I've committed Unto [A]Him against that day."
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]I know not how [G]this saving faith To [D]me He did impart,
[G]Nor how believing [D]in His word Wrought [A]peace within my heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]I know not [G]how the Spirit moves, [D]Convincing men of sin,
[G]Revealing Jesus through [D]the word, Creating [A]faith in Him.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]I know not when [G]my Lord may come, [D]At night or noonday fair,
[G]Nor if I walk [D]the vale with Him, Or [A]meet Him in the air.
{end_of_verse}
